    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before settlers, the Upper Chehalis called the area Tasunshun, meaning \"resting place\".",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fords_Prairie%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1800s, travelers stopped at the Halfway House, an inn built right on the wagon trail.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fords_Prairie%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Wesley Everest Gravesite in Fords Prairie is listed on the National Register of Historic Places since 1991.",
